<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

    <PropertyGroup>
        <Title>Stride Community Toolkit - Box2D Physics</Title>
        <Description>Box2D.NET physics integration for the Stride Community Toolkit - an experimental 2D physics alternative.

What's inside:
- Box2DSimulation: a Box2D world bound to Stride entities, with fixed-timestep stepping and transform sync
- Contact, hit and sensor events routed to your handlers via PhysicsEventRouter2D
- PhysicsQueries2D: closest-hit and all-hits raycasts, circle and segment shape casts, point, AABB and circle overlap queries
- ShapeFixtureBuilder: Box2D fixtures matching the toolkit's 2D primitives (box, circle, triangle, capsule) and chains
- Joints2D: revolute, prismatic, wheel, distance, weld, motor and filter joints from world-space anchors
- CharacterMover2D: a Quake-style platformer capsule on the v3 mover API, with no rigid body
- Grabber2DScript and Box2DDebugDraw: mouse pick-and-drag and the testbed's debug view through ShapeBatch
- SvgPath2D: straight-line SVG paths as chain points
- BodyForces: impulse and velocity helpers for bodies

Requires the Box2D.NET package.$(StrideVersionNote)</Description>
        <!-- Not published to NuGet yet: the API is still settling while Box2D support matures. -->
        <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <Import Project="..\CommonSettings.props" />

    <ItemGroup>
        <PackageReference Include="Box2D.NET" Version="3.1.654" />
    </ItemGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="..\Stride.CommunityToolkit\Stride.CommunityToolkit.csproj" />
        <!-- Box2DDebugDraw renders through ShapeBatch: the testbed look is the shape package. -->
        <ProjectReference Include="..\Stride.CommunityToolkit.Shapes\Stride.CommunityToolkit.Shapes.csproj" />
    </ItemGroup>


    <ItemGroup>
        <!-- JointFrames2D is internal; its frame arithmetic is pure and unit tested. -->
        <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Stride.CommunityToolkit.Tests" />
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>